        "approved": true,
        "value": "The main gathering I've attended is the Junior Science and Humanities Symposium, where I was a national finalist for my independent research on Valley Fever and environmental disease modeling. I built an SIR-style epidemiological model in Python and a microcontroller-based dust sensor for that project, and presenting it at JSHS was my first real experience defending technical work in front of people outside my own field.\n\nMore recently, most of my out-of-classroom exposure has come through programs rather than conferences: ClarityAtlas, the iOS health product I built and shipped into a live Hopkins pilot with 30+ users, was selected for the Johns Hopkins Pava Spark Accelerator and NSF I-Corps, both of which involved cohort sessions and customer-discovery interviews with people well outside Hopkins.\n\nI don't have specific conferences locked in for this year yet. I'd be interested in developer and applied-ML events if Stripe has a presence at any, and I'm happy to be pointed toward ones worth attending.",
